I have completed the analysis of the power network and generated the required report. I formulated the problem as a DC Optimal Power Flow (OPF) with spinning reserve requirements and solved it using Linear Programming. The results are stored in `report.json`, which includes individual generator dispatches, total costs, loads, generations, reserve allocations, the three most loaded transmission lines, and the remaining operating margin.

```json
{
  "generator_dispatch": [
    {"id": 1, "bus": 316, "output_MW": 476.0, "reserve_MW": 15.0, "pmax_MW": 491.0},
    ...
  ],
  "totals": {
    "cost_dollars_per_hour": 2965906.07,
    "load_MW": 144848.96,
    "generation_MW": 144848.96,
    "reserve_MW": 5923.5
  },
  "most_loaded_lines": [
    {"from": 1101, "to": 400, "loading_pct": 100.0},
    {"from": 91, "to": 200, "loading_pct": 100.0},
    {"from": 1660, "to": 2664, "loading_pct": 100.0}
  ],
  "operating_margin_MW": 68315.54
}
```
